meta {
  name: List posts
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/media?category={{category}}&tag={{tag}}&includeArchived={{includeArchived}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  category: {{category}}
  tag: {{tag}}
  includeArchived: {{includeArchived}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # List posts

  `GET /api/media`

  Return posts ordered by createdAt descending.

  ## Authentication

  Public.

  ## Parameters

  | Name | Location | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | category | Query | Example: `{{category}}`. |
  | tag | Query | Example: `{{tag}}`. |
  | includeArchived | Query | Example: `{{includeArchived}}`. |

  ## Request body

  No request body.

  ## Response

  HTTP **200**.

  ```json
  [
    {
      "id": "22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222",
      "title": "City mural",
      "description": "Session documentation",
      "category": "Graffiti",
      "hashtags": [
        "graffiti"
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
          "url": "https://example.com/mural.webp",
          "type": "image",
          "isCover": true,
          "thumbnailUrl": null
        }
      ],
      "isArchived": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-11-14T12:00:00Z",
      "mediaAssets": [
        {
          "id": "33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333",
          "url": "https://example.com/mural.webp",
          "type": "image",
          "isCover": true,
          "thumbnailUrl": null
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
  ```

  ## Errors

  - 400: invalid includeArchived boolean.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  Filters use AND. category is case-insensitive; tag is lowercased and matched as exact array membership. includeArchived defaults to false. Archived records can be included publicly. No pagination. Disable category/tag in Params to list all posts.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
